@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
    ViewData["Subtitle"] = "How we handle your data in the Contract Monthly Claim Portal";
}

<div class="page-head">
    <div>
        <h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
        <p class="page-sub">
            Contract Monthly Claim Portal – Lecturer, Coordinator, Manager and HR access
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row g-3">
    <div class="col-xl-8">
        <div class="glass-card">
            <h4 class="mb-3">1. Purpose of this system</h4>
            <p>
                The Contract Monthly Claim (CMC) Portal is used to capture, review and approve
                monthly claims for contract lecturers. Access is restricted to authorised users
                (Lecturer, Coordinator, Manager and HR roles).
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4 mb-3">2. Information we store</h4>
            <p>
                The system stores the minimum information required to manage the claim workflow,
                including:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Basic user details (name, email address and role).</li>
                <li>Lecturer profile details (for example hourly rate and contract information).</li>
                <li>Claim information (hours worked, rate at submission, calculated amount and status).</li>
                <li>Uploaded supporting documents related to specific claims.</li>
            </ul>

            <h4 class="mt-4 mb-3">3. How your information is used</h4>
            <p>
                Your information is used only to:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Allow you to sign in and access the correct dashboard for your role.</li>
                <li>Create, track and process monthly claims through the workflow.</li>
                <li>Provide supporting information for review, verification and approval.</li>
                <li>Generate reports or exports that support internal admin processes.</li>
            </ul>

            <h4 class="mt-4 mb-3">4. Storage and security</h4>
            <p>
                Claims and user records are stored in the system database. Supporting documents
                are stored in encrypted form on the server and are only decrypted when
                downloaded by authorised users as part of the claim review process.
            </p>
            <p>
                Access to the system is controlled by login credentials and role-based
                authorisation. Each user can only access screens and actions that match
                their assigned role.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4 mb-3">5. Access to your data</h4>
            <p>
                Access to information in this portal is limited as follows:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Lecturers</strong> can view and track their own claims and the status of those claims.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Coordinators</strong> can view and verify pending claims for lecturers they are
                    responsible for.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Managers</strong> can view and approve verified claims.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>HR</strong> can view claims and lecturer information required for payroll and reporting.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h4 class="mt-4 mb-3">6. Data retention</h4>
            <p>
                Claim and profile data is retained for as long as is necessary to support the
                internal academic and administrative processes it was captured for, or as
                required by internal policy and audit requirements.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4 mb-3">7. Your responsibilities</h4>
            <p>
                As a user of this system, you are responsible for:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Keeping your login details secure and not sharing them with others.</li>
                <li>Ensuring that the information you capture (for example hours worked) is accurate.</li>
                <li>Reporting any suspected unauthorised access or issues to the relevant administrator.</li>
            </ul>

            <h4 class="mt-4 mb-3">8. Questions</h4>
            <p>
                If you have questions about how your data is used in this portal, please contact
                the system administrator or your programme coordinator.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
